---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Label from "../components/Label.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../schema";
import { ORG, CONTACT, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE } from "../consts";

const schemas = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Terms of Service", path: "/terms" },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms governing use of the Website Support Studio website and managed service, operated by Corriston Consulting, LLC. Includes acceptable use, service disclaimers, and limitation of liability under Florida law."
  path="/terms"
  schemas={schemas}
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span><Label text="terms_of_service" /></span>
      </nav>
      <p class="kicker"><Label text="_legal" /></p>
      <h1><Label text="terms_of_service" /></h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);">Effective {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

      <div class="summary" style="margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <strong>Summary.</strong> These terms govern your use of the Website Support Studio website and
        managed service, operated by {ORG.legalName}. Paid engagements are governed by a separate service
        agreement; where it conflicts with these terms, the service agreement controls. The service is
        provided on an "as is" basis, and liability is limited as set out below. These terms are governed by
        the laws of the {ORG.jurisdiction}.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Agreement to terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using the Website Support Studio website or service (the "Service"), you agree to be
        bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you are using the Service on behalf of an
        organization, you represent that you are authorized to bind that organization, and "you" refers to
        that organization. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is operated by {ORG.legalName}, a limited liability company organized in the
        {" "}{ORG.jurisdiction}, with its principal place of business in {ORG.address.locality}, {ORG.address.region}.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The service and engagements</h2>
      <p>
        Website Support Studio is a managed website operations and support service. The specific scope,
        deliverables, response expectations, fees, and term of a paid engagement are defined in a separate
        written service agreement, order form, or statement of work ("Service Agreement"). These Terms
        govern your general use of the website and Service; in the event of a conflict between these Terms
        and a signed Service Agreement, the Service Agreement controls for that engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Customer responsibilities and acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree that you will:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>provide accurate information and the access required for us to perform requested work;</li>
        <li>hold the rights and permissions necessary for any content, credentials, or systems you submit to the desk;</li>
        <li>not submit unlawful, infringing, or malicious content, or content you are not authorized to share;</li>
        <li>not use the Service to violate any law or third-party right, to gain unauthorized access to any system, or to interfere with the integrity or performance of the Service;</li>
        <li>not attempt to circumvent the approval, security, or audit controls of the platform.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for activity
        under your account.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Approvals and authorized changes</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is built around a human approval gate: customer-facing changes are executed only after
        approval by an authorized approver. You are responsible for designating authorized approvers and for
        the decisions they make. We are not responsible for outcomes resulting from changes you or your
        authorized approvers direct or approve.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Website Support Studio name, logo, brand, website, and platform — including its design, text, and
        software — are owned by {ORG.legalName} and protected by applicable law. We grant you a limited,
        non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Service for your internal business purposes during
        your engagement. You retain ownership of the content and materials you provide to us; you grant us
        the rights necessary to use them to perform the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Fees</h2>
      <p>
        Fees, billing frequency, and payment terms are set out in your Service Agreement. Unless otherwise
        stated, fees are non-refundable. Late or failed payments may result in suspension of the Service in
        accordance with the Service Agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-party services and links</h2>
      <p>
        The Service relies on third-party providers (for example, hosting, database, payment, and email
        providers) and may link to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the content, policies,
        or practices of third parties, and your use of third-party services may be subject to their terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Service disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Except as expressly stated in a Service Agreement, the Service is provided "as is" and "as
        available", without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including any
        implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and
        non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that it
        will meet any particular requirement unless expressly agreed in a Service Agreement. The website and
        any content on it are provided for general informational purposes and do not constitute professional
        advice absent a signed engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, {ORG.legalName} and its owners, personnel, and providers
        will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive
        damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising out of or related to the
        Service, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. To the maximum extent permitted by law,
        our total aggregate liability arising out of or related to the Service will not exceed the greater of
        the amounts you paid to us for the Service in the three (3) months preceding the event giving rise to
        the claim, or one hundred U.S. dollars (US$100). Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations,
        so some of the above may not apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {ORG.legalName} from claims, damages, and expenses
        (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your content, your use of the Service, or your breach
        of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate access to the Service if you breach these Terms or your Service
        Agreement, or to protect the security or integrity of the Service. Provisions that by their nature
        should survive termination — including intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability,
        and governing law — will survive.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the {ORG.jurisdiction}, without regard to its conflict-of-law
        rules. The state and federal courts located in Florida will have exclusive jurisdiction over any
        dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Service, and you consent to their
        jurisdiction and venue.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. We will revise the effective date above and, where
        appropriate, provide additional notice. Continued use of the Service after an update constitutes
        acceptance of the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to {ORG.legalName} at
        {" "}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
